// @emit-error cannot be discriminated
// The `same-field-names-different-types-reject.vl` rule at the pair its exemption used to
// SWALLOW. `assignTags` refuses two variants that share a field-NAME set — `variantSig`, the
// tag key, IS that set — unless they are one variant reached through two spellings, and that
// exemption asked the wasm-type CODE per field. One code covers several VL types: `i32` and
// `boolean` are both code 0, so this pair presented as the layout-equal twin, both variants
// ranked tag 0, and both `is` tests lowered to the same `i32.const 0` compare. Measured on
// the branch without the identity column: `vl check` rc 0, `vl run` rc 0 printing `IS-P` for
// a value built through `Q` — a SILENT wrong answer, and the inverted spelling (the value
// built through `P`, tested `is Q`) is wrong the same way, so no construction decides it.
//
// The exemption now keys on the field's own type TEXT (`uFieldTyText`) rather than on how it
// STORES, so the pair joins `{a: i32} | {a: f64}` and `{a: i32} | {a: string}`. The
// layout-equal twin the exemption is FOR is unaffected — `variant-twin-scalar-spellings.vl`
// and `types/struct-union-same-shape*.vl` pin that side.
type P = { a: i32 }
type Q = { a: boolean }
const u: P | Q = { a: true }
if u is P { print("IS-P") } else { print("IS-Q") }
